== The Krastorio Prodigy: Modlist

Wave 2 is the capstone, and it plays by a different rule than the first two waves. The Castaway proved a factory can be built and launched a rocket; The Architect proved it can scale. *The Krastorio Prodigy* proves the engineer can master a factory that is *rebuilt* — every recipe rebalanced, every science tree replaced, combat turned into ballistics, and the win pushed to the very edge of the tech tree. This is the wave where *Space Age stays enabled*, and where the two anchors do the heavy lifting: *Krastorio 2*, the end-game-focused overhaul, and *Krastorio 2 Spaced Out*, the bridge that makes K2 run correctly with Space Age (K2's own page is explicit that without the bridge, "the game will load, but progression will be broken"). Together they form the most demanding and most rewarding setup this guide covers.

Nine mods ship in Wave 2. The wave's one rule is compatibility: every mod must be verified against the 2.0.77 target *and* against both anchors — K2's rebalanced recipes and the K2SO bridge. The strongest evidence in the whole wave belongs to three of the four officially recommended companions on the Krastorio 2 page, which ship here alongside the two overhauls. *Content* carries the four overhaul and content mods — Krastorio 2, Krastorio 2 Spaced Out, Krastorio 2 Imersite Asteroids and Armoured Biters. *Mechanics* carries the two system mods — FNEI and Fluid Must Flow. *Graphics* carries the three visual mods — Milestones, K2 Tech Card Icons for Space Age, and Krastorio2 - roboport mode colored textures. All nine are verified on the official Factorio Mod Portal; each card records its last-update date, its 2.0-line build, and its dependencies, and every verdict is logged in STATUS.md.

The Wave 0 QoL base carries into this wave. Even Distribution, Squeak Through 2, Rate Calculator, Factory Planner, YARM, Todo List and Bottleneck Lite were each re-verified against K2 for this chapter: all seven are pure client, UI or informational mods that cannot touch K2's rebalanced recipes (Rate Calculator and Factory Planner read the game's real data, so they see K2's recipes exactly as the game does; YARM monitors any resource patch including the new ores). Each carry-in verdict is logged in STATUS.md. The Wave 1 content and system mods — Miniloader, Deadlock's beltboxes, Warehousing, Cybersyn, Alien Biomes and the rest — deliberately do *not* carry: the content mods are recipe-adjacent and K2 rebalances every recipe, and this wave keeps its install deliberately focused on the two overhauls, their verified companions, and the carried QoL base rather than the Wave 1 scaling stack.
